 61TI2c  Phys Rev Lett 135, 232511 (2025)                                       
 61TI c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL) January 4, 2026                  
 61TI c  {+61}Ti was produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility                        
 61TI2c  using the {+9}Be({+70}Zn,X) reaction at E=352 MeV/nucleon. Target was  
 61TI3c  8-mm thick {+9}Be. BigRIPS was tuned to optimize transmission of       
 61TI4c  {+55}Ca, which was incident on alternately a carbon target and a       
 61TI5c  target frame. The identification of the nuclide of interest was        
 61TI6c  made in the BigRIPS separator by determining the atomic number and the 
 61TI7c  mass-to-charge ratio of the ion using the tof-B|r-|DE method. The      
 61TI8c  reaction products were transported through the ZeroDegree Spectrometer 
 61TI9c  and implanted into the ZeroDegree Advanced Decay Station (ZD-ADS).     
 61TIac  The ZD-ADS is composed of an implantation detector, LaBr{-3} detectors,
 61TIbc  a neutron tof array and a veto detector. Measured: implanted           
 61TIcc  ion-|b{+-}-t, implanted ion-|b{+-}-|g-t and implanted ions-|g-t        
 61TIdc  correlations.                                                          
 61TIec  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
 61TI  L 0.0                           7 MS      3                              
 61TI2 L %B-=100                                                                
 61TI cL %B-$Only |b{+-} decay mode is expected.                                
 61TI cL T$From a fit to the implanted ion-|b{+-}-t spectrum using the          
 61TI2cL unbinned maximum-likelihood method. The data analysis                  
 61TI3cL included contributions from the parent, daughter and grand-daughter    
 61TI4cL decays, as well as a constant background. Uncertainty includes both    
 61TI5cL statistical and systematic components.                                 
                                                                                
